Introduction                                                                                                   

This document collects the scientific literature regarding Artificial_General_Intelligence.                    


Recent Developments in AGI Research                                                                            

Policy, Ethics, and Societal Impact                                                                            

Recent discourse emphasizes the need for conceptual discipline and ethical frameworks surrounding AGI          
development. The European Commission's call for AGI in healthcare has sparked debate on risk management and the
precautionary principle, highlighting that the term "AGI" is often contested and potentially problematic when  
applied to advanced AI without clear boundaries[^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183]. Furthermore, critical analyses    
point out that the pursuit of AGI is sometimes rooted in normative frameworks linked to historical eugenicist  
ideologies, warning that undefined "safe AGI" systems could centralize power and harm marginalized groups under
the guise of benefiting humanity[^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636].                                                     

Architectural and Theoretical Foundations                                                                      

Theoretical advancements continue to explore the mathematical and topological underpinnings of autonomous      
intelligence. New frameworks propose replacing subjective units with formal morphogenetic structures to        
describe the transition from computation to genuine autonomy, arguing for the mathematical inevitability of AGI
through topological integrity and structural absorption of                                                     
energy[^10.5281_zenodo.19034234][^10.5281_zenodo.19034233]. Concurrently, research into the future of          
intelligence examines the philosophical movements of trans- and posthumanism, outlining how cognitive          
enhancements and brain-computer interfaces might converge with artificial super-intelligence to reshape human  
psychological capacities[^10.1016_j.intell.2021.101563].                                                       

Safety, Control, and Strategic Development                                                                     

Ensuring the controllability of powerful AGI systems remains a paramount challenge. Proposals for "provably    
safe systems" advocate for advanced formal verification and mechanistic interpretability as the only viable    
path to guaranteeing that AGI satisfies human-specified requirements[^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933]. Strategic    
monitoring efforts, such as those tracking China's national AI strategy, identify key institutions pursuing    
general AI capable of autonomous action in novel circumstances, emphasizing machine learning and brain-inspired
architectures[^10.51593_20210064]. Additionally, discussions on the neural network revolution highlight the    
necessity of transitioning from imitation-based problem solving to environmental interaction to bridge the gap 
between narrow AI and general intelligence[^10.20948_future-2023-16].                                          

Robotics, Consciousness, and Cognitive Integration                                                             

The intersection of robotics, consciousness, and AGI is increasingly scrutinized. Investigations into robot    
consciousness question whether sufficiently advanced general robotic intelligence could be indistinguishable   
from human consciousness, exploring implications for ethics, free will, and cosmological                       
ontologies[^10.22339_jbh.v7i4.7403]. Parallel inquiries into AI consciousness debate the potential for         
artificial systems to achieve genuine subjective experience, framing it as a central speculative frontier in   
the field[^10.1109_mpuls.2024.3354609]. Finally, deep reinforcement learning frameworks are being adapted as   
general-purpose architectures for intelligent robot control, aiming to create platform-independent high-level  
control systems that incrementally improve intelligence through environmental                                  
feedback[^10.48550_arxiv.2105.13806].                                                                          

